title: NetApp StorageGRID Tenant Quota
agents: special-agent(netapp_storagegrid)
catalog: os/storage
license: GPLv2
distribution: check_mk
description:
 This check monitors the object storage quota usage of a NetApp
 StorageGRID tenant account (Storage Tenant Account / Organization), as
 reported by the Grid Management REST API
 ({GET /api/v3/grid/accounts-cache}).

 One service is discovered per tenant account. The service reports the
 percentage of the tenant's configured object quota
 ({policy.quotaObjectBytes}) that is currently used
 ({dataBytes}). The monitoring state is derived from configurable
 WARN/CRIT levels on this percentage, via the "NetApp StorageGRID tenant
 quota" rule set. By default, the state is WARN at 80% and CRIT at 90%.

 Tenants that do not have a quota configured are always reported OK,
 since there is nothing to exceed.

 The used bytes, and, if a quota is configured, the quota bytes and the
 percentage used, are reported as performance data
 ({netapp_storagegrid_tenant_used_bytes},
 {netapp_storagegrid_tenant_quota_bytes},
 {netapp_storagegrid_tenant_quota_used_percent}).

 Note: tenant usage data in the StorageGRID cache can take up to 15
 minutes to reflect recent changes.

item:
 The display name of the tenant account. Tenant account names are only
 guaranteed to be unique by StorageGRID convention, not enforced by the
 API.

discovery:
 One service is created per tenant account.
